💡 **SUGGESTION: pin the new regex seams with a few edge-case tests**

The new pattern `(?<![:/\w])\.{0,2}/[\w./-]+\.(?:md|txt|json|yaml|yml)\b` is correct — verified against 25 boundary probes — but its three changes (lookbehind, dot in charset, trailing `\b`) interact in ways the current tests don't pin down. These are exactly the seams a future charset tweak would regress. Cases worth adding to `test/agents/instruction_processor_packpath_test.dart`:

```dart
test('trailing punctuation does not swallow the final dot', () {
  // "/p/a.md." must match "/p/a.md", leaving the sentence dot intact
  // (greedy [\w./-]+ backtracks off the trailing '.').
});

test('unknown longer extensions are not partially matched', () {
  // "/f/file.mdx" must match NOTHING — the trailing \b rejects the
  // old pattern's partial "/f/file.md" match.
});

test('host with trailing dot still not treated as a file path', () {
  // "https://x.com./readme.md": the lookbehind class excludes ':' '/' \w
  // but not '.', so "/readme.md" still matches — document as an accepted
  // boundary (embed only fires if /readme.md exists locally).
});

test('ellipsis before a path matches ../, not the literal dir', () {
  // ".../a.md" matches as "../a.md" (\.{0,2} is capped at 2 dots) —
  // pre-existing, but worth locking so a charset change can't widen it.
});
```

All four were probed against the merged regex; behavior today is: `/p/a.md.` → `/p/a.md` ✅, `/f/file.mdx` → no match ✅ (improvement over the old pattern), `https://x.com./readme.md` → matches `/readme.md` (contrived, harmless without a local file), `.../a.md` → `../a.md` (pre-existing). Purely test additions — no product change requested.

